A||N||1||MR2KLR||Aux Oil pres. Gauge & Fuel pump (Related?)||||1||
Z||000000||MR2KLR||11-26-2001||07:49 AM||||<BR>I just brought home my 88 coupe (With a bad pump?) last night the old owner has instaled a aux gauge pod. Does that tie in to the oil pressure switch? if the gauge is not instaled right will the fuel pump not run? how do I check the oil presure switch?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.tripod.com/wawoonigootphet/images/af/3in1_vu1.jpg">  <A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOY/" TARGET=_blank>Tom's Page</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||11-26-2001||09:06 AM||||The installation of an aux. pod in any '86 thru '88 is plug and play. No need to splice anything so it can't be screwed-up. (unless whoever does it doesn't know)<BR>To check your oil pressure, remove sending unit and replace with a manual gauge, then compare your reading.<BR>Fuel pump problems?<BR>Check fuse (visual), check relay (listen for 'click' when key is turned to 'run'-that's about it.<BR>If your car runs when primed and stalls chances are good for a bad fuel pump.<BR>Hope this helps.||||reg||1
